  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1999-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Write \\[ \\begin{aligned} 2^{1999} \\cdot 5^{2001} &= 2^{1999} \\cdot 5^{1999} \\cdot 5^2 \\\\ &= 25 \\cdot 10^{1999}, \\end{aligned} \\] which is \\(25\\) followed by \\(1999\\) zeros. The sum of the digits is \\(2 + 5 = 7.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Pair each factor of \\(2\\) with a factor of \\(5\\) to make \\(10\\)",
        "\\(2^{1999} \\cdot 5^{2001} = 5^2 \\cdot 10^{1999}\\)"
      ],
